From: Dreyk <dreyksmail@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 16:10:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mtk_ppe: keep the L2 flow when one of its subflows ends

A bridged (L2) flow offloaded through tc flower, e.g. by bridger, is a
parent entry keyed by the MAC pair; __mtk_ppe_check_skb() binds every
connection between the two hosts as a subflow of it.

Since "net: ethernet: mtk_eth_soc: improve keeping track of offloaded
flows" mtk_flow_entry_update_l2() clears the parent instead of the
subflow whose hardware entry is no longer bound. The first connection
that ends (TCP FIN, ageing, a hash collision) thus removes the parent
from l2_flows and frees all of its subflows: the other connections stop
being tracked, and every new connection between the two hosts finds no
parent and stays on the CPU while the tc rule still exists.

Clear only the stale subflow, as before that change.

---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_ppe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_ppe.c
@@ -643,7 +643,7 @@ mtk_flow_entry_update_l2(struct mtk_ppe
 		if (!mtk_flow_entry_update(ppe, cur, packets, bytes)) {
 			entry->prev_packets += cur->prev_packets;
 			entry->prev_bytes += cur->prev_bytes;
-			__mtk_foe_entry_clear(ppe, entry, false);
+			__mtk_foe_entry_clear(ppe, cur, false);
 			continue;
 		}
 
